-- SHADOWING ----------------------------- qa/NotificationAnnouncementReplay.elm

The name `serial` is first defined here:

17| serial root = D.decodeValue (D.field "announcement" (D.field "sequence" UInt64.decoder)) (Outputs.frame root) |> Result.withDefault UInt64.zero
    ^^^^^^
But then it is defined AGAIN over here:

31| pointer owner serial state = E.object [("protocolVersion",E.int 3),("kind",E.string "pointer-ownership"),("ownershipProtocol",E.int 1),("binding",owner),("requestId",E.string "1"),("serial",E.string serial),("state",E.string state),("owner",if state=="idle" then E.null else E.string "7")]
                  ^^^^^^
Think of a more helpful name for one of them and you should be all set!

Note: Linters advise against shadowing, so Elm makes “best practices” the
default. Read <https://elm-lang.org/0.19.2/shadowing> for more details on this
choice.

